      "answer": {
        "coverage": "complete",
        "insufficient_evidence": false,
        "summary": "Expert-led post-training can fuel fast growth because AI labs are willing to invest heavily in better model capabilities, and expert labor helps solve a critical bottleneck: defining and measuring success. The work is valuable, ongoing, and can scale from high-quality specialist teams into a large labor marketplace; Mercor’s reported growth illustrates the demand.",
        "summary_citation_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S3",
          "S6",
          "S7"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "It addresses a costly model-improvement bottleneck",
            "content": "Foody says top AI labs need professionals who can measure model capabilities, and that improving models is bottlenecked by having an effective way to define what success looks like. Labs are willing to spend heavily to improve capabilities. Experts create evaluations and post-training data that guide models toward desired capabilities; for example, radiologists can help establish diagnoses and associated rewards or penalties, influencing the quality of the model’s recommendations.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1",
              "S2",
              "S3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "The work can support a large, durable market",
            "content": "Foody describes evaluations as evergreen: labs need experts to measure success across the domains they want models to handle, even if training methods change. He says tens of thousands of people may be working on this at a given time, and hundreds of thousands more generally. He also argues that higher-caliber workers can achieve more with smaller teams initially, then scale up after meeting the quality bar.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S2",
              "S3",
              "S4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Marketplace economics and reported growth",
            "content": "The opportunity is not just one-off expert advice: Foody distinguishes longer project-based work from a single expert-network call, with a labor-marketplace model for retaining and engaging skilled contributors. Mercor’s reported revenue run rate grew from $1 to $400 million in 16 months, which Foody called the fastest ascent in history; he presents that growth in the context of working with top AI labs.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S6",
              "S7"
            ]
          }
